{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdjacencyList"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertex set is any set of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" values. The edge set is a set of ordered pairs of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot. Edges are kept in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so an edge’s position in "},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"code":"0..<edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a weight can live"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in an array beside the graph. Each slot has a row of the slots of its out-neighbors, a parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row of those edges’ positions, and a row of its in-neighbors; the rows of each kind share one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(amortized, like "},{"code":"Array","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and copying it copies a constant number of buffers. A dictionary from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slot pair to position answers "},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in O(1)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"AdjacencyListModule"}],"title":"AdjacencyList","externalID":"s:19AdjacencyListModule0aB0V","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":"AdjacencyList.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList.swift#L20"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AdjacencyList"}]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/Neighbors"]},{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init()","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(_:)-2unw2","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(_:)-6cbnw","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList\/init(adjacency:)","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/Adja